      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>In the web console, navigate to <strong>Ecosystem</strong> -&gt; <strong>Installed Operators</strong>.</li>
      <li>Under the <strong>Provided APIs</strong> heading for the <strong>Network Observability Operator</strong>, select <strong>Flow Collector</strong>.</li>
      <li>Select <strong>cluster</strong>, and then select the <strong>YAML</strong> tab.</li>
      <li>
      Increase the <code>spec.agent.ebpf.cacheMaxFlows</code> value, as shown in the following YAML sample:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: flows.netobserv.io/v1beta2\nkind: FlowCollector\nmetadata:\n  name: cluster\nspec:\n  namespace: netobserv\n  deploymentModel: Service\n  agent:\n    type: eBPF\n    ebpf:\n      cacheMaxFlows: 200000"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>spec.agent.ebpf.cacheMaxFlows</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the maximum number of flows to cache. If a <code>NetObservAgentFlowsDropped</code> alert occurs, increase this value from its current level.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      </li>
      </ol>
